description: Privacy, security, and health-data handling rules
alwaysApply: true
---

# Privacy & security

- No secrets, API keys, or service-role keys in git.
- No real patient/health PII in fixtures, screenshots committed to repo, or logs.
- Prefer least-privilege access; family data needs explicit permission model.
- Product copy must not diagnose or promise medical outcomes.
- Account deletion / data export are product requirements, not afterthoughts (DPDP).
- Client-only storage of sensitive health records is not an acceptable Foundation architecture.
